# Every base image this repository builds on, named exactly once.
#
# The Dockerfiles take these as build arguments rather than writing a `FROM`
# line each, which buys two things. An operator mirroring images into an
# air-gapped registry has one list to read. And `tools/check_image_pinning.py`
# has one file to check, so "no image floats" is a build failure rather than a
# review comment somebody has to remember to make.
#
# Two rules, both enforced:
#
#   - No `latest`, and no bare major version. A tag that moves is a build that
#     is not reproducible, and the failure arrives on a morning nobody changed
#     anything.
#   - Once a digest is added, it must be well-formed and stay attached. Pin the
#     digests for a release with `sh deploy/images/pin.sh`, which resolves each
#     tag against the registry the operator actually pulls from — this file
#     ships with tags because a digest written by hand is a digest nobody
#     verified, and one that resolves to nothing fails a build at the worst
#     moment.

# Builds the wheel and runs it. One image for both stages: the build stage is
# discarded, and having the runtime differ from the thing the wheel was built
# against is how a C extension comes to be missing at start.
BASE_PYTHON=python:3.12.11-slim-bookworm

# The one datastore. Apache AGE's own image, which pins the PostgreSQL major
# version its extension was compiled against; pgvector is added on top from
# PGDG. No published image carries both.
BASE_POSTGRES=apache/age:release_PG16_1.6.0

# The sandbox's egress sidecar in the kubernetes profile. Its allow-list is what
# makes "the agent reached only what it was permitted to" enforceable rather
# than asserted.
BASE_ENVOY=envoyproxy/envoy:v1.32.3
